      "text": " \nTo find the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\), we perform long division:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.1} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9} \\\\\n\\cline{2-2}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{10} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nWe continue the division:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.14} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9.0} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{100} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.142} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9.00} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{100.0} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.1428} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9.000} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{100.00} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.14285} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9.0000} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{100.000} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c|ccccccc}\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{0.142857} \\\\\n\\cline{2-8}\n7 & 1.000000000 \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{9.00000} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{100.0000} \\\\\n\\multicolumn{2}{r}{} \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\nThus, the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\( 0.\\overline{142857} \\). The repeating block is \"142857\" with a length of 6 digits.\n\nTo find the 100th digit after the decimal point, we determine the position of the 100th digit within the repeating block. We do this by finding the remainder of 100 divided by 6:\n\n\\[\n100 \\div 6 = 16 \\text{ remainder } 4\n\\]\n\nThis tells us that the 100th digit corresponds to the 4th digit in the repeating block \"142857\". The 4th digit in \"142857\" is 2.\n\nTherefore, the 100th digit after the decimal point of the decimal representation of \\( \\frac{1}{7} \\) is \\(\\boxed{2}\\).",
